

In the event of multiple GPU cards installed be sure to check the
bullshit NVidia "compute" level crap number which determines the
version of the internal PTX code base to build into the output
binary blob.

see https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-gpus
also https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda/gpus/legacy

For normal humans without $MILLIONS$ to blow on bullshit
hardware you will likely need compute_60 as a minimum
in the year 2026. Good fucking luck. The drop in type
replacement for the legacy GP100 seems to be the A100.

At this time ( July 2026 ) the 40G memory A100 is $5000.

Be sure to use a g++ compiler that CUDA does not barf all over.

This means GCC 12.x or maybe 13.x and good luck with 14.x ver.

$ echo $PATH
/usr/local/cuda-12.9/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/opt/bw/bin:/opt/bw/sbin:/bin:/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/sbin:/opt/schily/bin
$ 

$ nvcc -x cu -ccbin /usr/bin/g++-12 -I../include \
-I/usr/local/cuda-12.9/include \
-gencode arch=compute_60,code=sm_60 \
-Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets \
-lnppi_static -lculibos -c -o dev_info.o dev_info.cu

$ nvcc -ccbin /usr/bin/g++-12 -I../include \
-gencode arch=compute_60,code=sm_60 \
-Wno-deprecated-gpu-targets -o dev_info dev_info.o 

-----------------------------------------------------------
With CUDA 12.9, V12.9.86 this may look like legacy behavior
for reasons unknown :

t# /usr/local/cuda-12.9/bin/nvcc --version
nvcc: NVIDIA (R) Cuda compiler driver
Copyright (c) 2005-2025 NVIDIA Corporation
Built on Tue_May_27_02:21:03_PDT_2025
Cuda compilation tools, release 12.9, V12.9.86
Build cuda_12.9.r12.9/compiler.36037853_0
t# 

t# nvidia-smi -pm 1                
Enabled Legacy persistence mode for GPU 00000000:02:00.0.
Enabled Legacy persistence mode for GPU 00000000:81:00.0.
All done.
t# nvidia-smi --gpu-reset
GPU Reset couldn't run because GPU 00000000:02:00.0 is the primary GPU.
t# 


In the past we may see :

# nvidia-smi --gpu-reset
GPU 00000000:01:00.0 was successfully reset.
All done.

